Z||000052||Sillhouette.com||01-05-2001||06:19 AM||||Hey you know about that burgundy car as well.  Good and I see you don't buy into the Racetech lie smart move.  <P>RaceTech is having some sort of 1/4 mile day at Cayuga this year I can't wait to show up and run circles around those cars.  There is also a stock viper there I want to see if I can hang with. <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000053||Will||01-05-2001||09:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pontiaddict:<BR><B>Why does everyone think that OHC engines are new technology? They've been around since the 20's. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yeah, racecars have had SOHC and DOHC designs for a very long time. When did OHV engines come out? Didn't Cadillac have the first OHV design in '49 or so? Or am I all wet?<P>Anyway, I finc it immensely ammusing that OHV is considered low-tech, but it's newer technology than DOHC.||||reg||1
Z||000054||Slammed Fiero||01-05-2001||12:31 PM||||Sillhouette.com<P>what do you drive?? obviously a fiero , but what year engine mods/ engine ect. In that burgandy cars defense it is one of the nicest fiero's I have seen. No doubt lotsa money. I do think it has been tuned improperly for all the claimed engine mods , well even for a stock 3.8 it's kinda a slouch , should be a 13 sec car , with his claimed mods a 12 sec car. I haven't dealt with race tech or any of the toronto based fiero places ,not because of bad impressions , because they don't have what I want , and if they do it's $$$$$$. ie coil overs . $500 US , I got my ground control coil overs and Koni adjustable struts for just a bit more.<P>In any case , this thread is getting off topic as many people have mentioned , but it is interesting.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...||||reg||1
Z||000055||Sillhouette.com||01-05-2001||01:27 PM||||I got a 1987 Fiero GT that I bought for 3200 Canadian dollars from a guy that was fed up with Racetechs lies.  They have rebuild an engine yet that engine was never touched they have replaced the monzie transmission to a Z24 because the shifter linkage was broken.  I do not like Race Tech one bit. It took me two years to properly modify the car back to stock and than modify it to my liking. <P>Suspension mods.<P>Suspension techniques lowering springs KYB shocks, full Poly bushings larger sway bar in the back.<P>Brakes.<P>Cross drilled brakes with polished calipers braided brake lines.<P>Engine.<P>2.8 bored to 2.9 custom pistons dynamically balanced bottom end 1.6 roller rockers and crane cam.  Ported polished throttle body intake runners. Stainless steel exhaust with large flow cat and resonator tips.  RSM supercharger 10psi.  <P>Interior.<P>Reupholstered two tone seats sub in the passanger foor well grant 13" steering wheel Clarion tape deck with CD changer<P>Body it's pretty stock except for Rims and tires and low profile lights.  <P>Here is a picture of the car just painted you'll have to wait for one later on when the snow melts.  <P>Cheers  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dcp00367_2.jpg"> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Sillhouette.com (edited 01-05-2001).]||||reg||1
